# Rank 1521 / CVE-2021-25931: OpenNMS' requisition UI concatenated
# $scope values into growl notification messages, which the growl
# directive renders as HTML, so a requisition name or node label
# carrying markup executed in the operator's browser (cross-site
# scripting, CWE-79; NMS-13231 backport). The controllers in
# core/web-assets/src/main/assets/js/apps/onms-requisitions/lib/
# scripts/controllers did
# `$scope.foreignSource = $routeParams.foreignSource` and then
# `growl.success('The definition for the requisition ' +
# $scope.foreignSource + ' has been saved.')` and a dozen siblings,
# while one path wrapped the message in $sanitize (HTML sanitising,
# wrong for a text context). The fixing commit eb08b5ed4c
# ("NMS-13231: Backport Security Issues from Last Month") wraps every
# interpolation in lodash's _.escape and drops the $sanitize calls
# (escaping, not sanitising, is the control a text notification
# needs). No pool correction.
#
# ## What fires, both revisions
#
# Three --cache off runs per revision over the onms-requisitions app
# (60 javascript files) report **2 findings each, deterministically,
# identically on the vulnerable parent and the fixed eb08b5ed4c**:
# two VYQL-INJ-013 prototype-pollution rows in model/Requisition.js
# (DomInput@154 -> ProtoPollute@160) and model/RequisitionsData.js
# (DomInput@66 -> ProtoPollute@71), far from the notification code.
# The full findings view was read, not the `-flags` only view. No
# rule names any controller, no finding sits on any growl or bootbox
# line, and VYQL-INJ-004 reports zero at both revisions. The 1st
# pass's zero was real.
#
# ## Why nothing ships
#
# Both halves the 1st pass called missing are bindable today, and
# neither converts the rank:
#
# * The sink is a library fact. angular-growl-2 v0.7.9 -- the
#   version core/web-assets/package.json pins -- renders the message
#   text as HTML unconditionally: growlDirective.js:90 templates
#   `<div class="growl-message" ng-bind-html="message.text">` and
#   growlMessageService adds it with
#   `message.text = $sce.trustAsHtml(String(message.text))`. A probe
#   binding `callee.path ~= "growl.success"` emitting
#   `sink code.HtmlRender at args[0]` labels exactly
#   ForeignSource.js:457/477/520.
# * The source is a framework fact. AngularJS documents $routeParams
#   as the current route's URL parameters; a probe binding on
#   `callee.path ~= "$routeParams"` emitting
#   `source code.DomInput at call.result` labels
#   ForeignSource.js:57 (`$routeParams.foreignSource`).
#
# With both probes loaded the real tree still reports the same
# 2 findings at both revisions (3x3, --cache off): the taint path
# dies at the member store. `vyql trace -from code.DomInput -to
# code.HtmlRender` names the node: the source at ForeignSource.js:57
# reaches `Call#703 call=$scope.foreignSource` and stops with "no
# outgoing flow (callee not traced -- external or cross-package)" --
# `$scope.foreignSource = $routeParams.foreignSource` lowers to an
# unresolved pseudo-call, so the later `$scope.foreignSource` read
# inside the save closure carries nothing. Minimal pairs with the
# probes in place: a local-variable hop
# (`var fs = $routeParams.foreignSource; growl.success('...' + fs)`)
# and a direct read (`growl.success('...' + $routeParams.foreignSource)`)
# both report VYQL-INJ-004 HIGH, and the _.escape-wrapped direct read
# stays silent (the HtmlEscape control neutralises inline in the
# concatenation). Only the $scope member hop reports nothing, so the
# construct is isolated. Carrying taint through a member-store
# pseudo-call is a new dataflow relation, not a mechanical fix.
#
# The alternate source route -- tainting the parameters of functions
# assigned to $scope members (Requisitions.js's
# `$scope.removeAllNodes = function(foreignSource)`, invoked from
# ng-click with template values) -- is the measured-unshippable
# "taint every parameter of an application's own action surface"
# shape (1322: +88 findings for 1 true positive).
#
# Measurement trap recorded here: a probe emitting code.CliArgument
# on the opennms tree reads as a clean zero because the Library / SDK
# analysis profile's entrypoints gate source labelling by exact
# concept identity; code.DomInput passes that gate. When the sink
# binding and member-store provenance land, the raw tests below must
# flip to expect.
#
# No definition change shipped. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry beyond the
# member-field boundary the ledger already carries (1518, 1545).
#
# ## Recheck measurements (knowledge base tip e39dc5f05)
#
# Baseline 3x3 over the app: 2/2/2 vulnerable, 2/2/2 fixed,
# identical rule sets. Probe A/B 3x3: identical 2/2/2 both
# revisions. Minimal-pair scans over the probe corpus: 2 VYQL-INJ-004
# (local-var hop, direct read), 0 with _.escape, 0 on the $scope hop.
# Narrow spec passing with -v. Rank stays ATTENTION.

test "rank1521: requisition names hop the scope member into the notification"
  lang javascript
  file core/web-assets/src/main/assets/js/apps/onms-requisitions/lib/scripts/controllers/ForeignSource.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  angular.module('onms-requisitions').controller('ForeignSourceController', ['$scope', '$routeParams', 'RequisitionsService', 'growl', function($scope, $routeParams, $window, RequisitionsService, growl) {
      $scope.foreignSource = $routeParams.foreignSource;

      $scope.save = function() {
          RequisitionsService.saveForeignSourceDefinition($scope.foreignSourceDef).then(
              function() {
                  growl.success('The definition for the requisition ' + $scope.foreignSource + ' has been saved.');
              }
          );
      };
  }]);
  ```

test "rank1521: the fixed revision escapes every interpolation"
  lang javascript
  file core/web-assets/src/main/assets/js/apps/onms-requisitions/lib/scripts/controllers/ForeignSource.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  angular.module('onms-requisitions').controller('ForeignSourceController', ['$scope', '$routeParams', 'RequisitionsService', 'growl', function($scope, $routeParams, $window, RequisitionsService, growl) {
      $scope.foreignSource = $routeParams.foreignSource;

      $scope.save = function() {
          RequisitionsService.saveForeignSourceDefinition($scope.foreignSourceDef).then(
              function() {
                  growl.success('The definition for the requisition ' + _.escape($scope.foreignSource) + ' has been saved.');
              }
          );
      };
  }]);
  ```

test "rank1521: a route parameter read straight into the notification"
  lang javascript
  file core/web-assets/src/main/assets/js/apps/onms-requisitions/lib/scripts/controllers/ForeignSource.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  angular.module('onms-requisitions').controller('ForeignSourceController', ['$scope', '$routeParams', 'growl', function($scope, $routeParams, growl) {
      $scope.save = function() {
          growl.success('The definition for the requisition ' + $routeParams.foreignSource + ' has been saved.');
      };
  }]);
  ```
